    {
      "id": "s3",
      "part": 3,
      "label": "Part 3",
      "instruction": "Talk together with your partner about the situation.",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "q3",
          "number": 3,
          "points": 20,
          "skills": [],
          "material": [
            {
              "id": "i2",
              "type": "imageRef",
              "image": "img2"
            }
          ],
          "interaction": {
            "kind": "speaking",
            "prompt": [
              {
                "t": "text",
                "v": "Talk with your partner about the different ways a boy could improve his English before a short holiday in England, and decide which would be best."
              }
            ],
            "turns": [
              {
                "id": "t1",
                "text": "Now, in this part of the test you’re going to talk about something together for about two minutes. I’m going to describe a situation to you. A boy is going to visit England soon for a short holiday. He wants to improve his English quickly before he goes. Here are some ways he could improve his English. Talk together about the different ways he could improve his English before his holiday and say which would be best. All right? Now, talk together.",
                "role": "examiner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet2/pet2-t1-s-q3-t1.mp3",
                  "seconds": 33.3
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t2",
                "text": "Shall I start? I think an English class is a good idea, because a teacher can correct his mistakes. What do you think?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet2/pet2-t1-s-q3-t2.mp3",
                  "seconds": 7.7
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t3",
                "text": "That’s true. What about listening to songs in English? It’s fun, and he can do it every day. Do you agree?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet2/pet2-t1-s-q3-t3.mp3",
                  "seconds": 7.5
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t4",
                "text": "I’m not sure about studying alone with a book. It could be a bit boring, and he won’t practise speaking. What’s your opinion?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet2/pet2-t1-s-q3-t4.mp3",
                  "seconds": 7.5
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t5",
                "text": "What about watching films in English or using an app on his phone? Which one do you think is more useful?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet2/pet2-t1-s-q3-t5.mp3",
                  "seconds": 6.4
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t6",
                "text": "He hasn’t got much time, so maybe a private teacher is better. He can practise speaking a lot. What do you think?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet2/pet2-t1-s-q3-t6.mp3",
                  "seconds": 7.1
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t7",
                "text": "So, which way do you think would be best for him? I think the private teacher, because it helps quickly.",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet2/pet2-t1-s-q3-t7.mp3",
                  "seconds": 6.2
                }
              }
            ],
            "maxSeconds": 45,
            "scoring": "judge"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
